T8020: add APRR support, disable PMAP code signing, stub IOMMU helper

A12 (T8020) was the first Apple chip with APRR (Access Permission
Remap Registers), the hardware feature that PPL's XPRR permission
system requires.  Without __APRR_SUPPORTED__, all XPRR constants,
APRR register names, and PPL lockdown functions are undefined --
causing ~30 compilation errors across pmap, locore, and start.s.

Disable PMAP_CS (PPL-based Code Signing) because the full PMAP_CS
infrastructure (pmap_cs_blob, pmap_cs_main, trust-cache dispatch
indices, and the code-signing acceleration buffer) ships only in
Apple's closed per-SoC library.  Combined with the SEP fallback in
patch 0002, code signing validation falls back to the non-PPL path.

Also add a macro stub for ptep_get_iommu() -- the closed-source
DART IOMMU helper that returns the IOMMU device owning a PTE.
The stub returns the raw PTE pointer, which is sufficient for the
diagnostic panic messages that reference it.

diff --git a/pexpert/pexpert/arm64/H12.h b/pexpert/pexpert/arm64/H12.h
--- a/pexpert/pexpert/arm64/H12.h
+++ b/pexpert/pexpert/arm64/H12.h
@@ -44,6 +44,15 @@
 #define CPU_HAS_APPLE_PAC        1 /* A12 is the FIRST Apple PAC/arm64e chip -- public, well-documented fact */
 #define __ARM_PAN_AVAILABLE__    1 /* ARMv8.1 PAN, below A12's baseline */

+#define __APRR_SUPPORTED__       1 /* A12 introduced APRR -- the permission
+                                    * remapping that PPL (XNU_MONITOR) needs.
+                                    * Without this, XPRR constants and APRR
+                                    * system register names are undefined. */
+
+/* Stub: ptep_get_iommu is in Apple's closed DART IOMMU library.
+ * Returns the raw PTE pointer -- sufficient for diagnostic messages. */
+#define ptep_get_iommu(pte_p) ((void *)(pte_p))
+
 #define HAS_KTRR                 1 /* NOT HAS_CTRR -- CTRR is H13+ (A14-and-newer) only; KTRR is the
                                      * explicit predecessor fallback still wired in current XNU's
                                      * apple_arm64_common.h (HAS_CTRR3 -> HAS_CTRR -> HAS_KTRR -> MONITOR),
diff --git a/pexpert/pexpert/arm64/board_config.h b/pexpert/pexpert/arm64/board_config.h
--- a/pexpert/pexpert/arm64/board_config.h
+++ b/pexpert/pexpert/arm64/board_config.h
@@ -114,9 +114,7 @@
 #define MAX_L2_CLINE                   7
 #define MAX_CPUS                       6   /* 2 Vortex (perf) + 4 Tempest (eff) -- confirmed against XR's real ADT, see ../../research/devicetree-xr.md */
 #define MAX_CPU_CLUSTERS               2

-#define PMAP_CS                        1
-#define PMAP_CS_ENABLE                 1
 #define XNU_MONITOR                    1 /* Secure pmap runtime */
 #endif  /* ARM64_BOARD_CONFIG_T8020 */

